*  X12 [X] value/defer element inside an INVOKED proc: m3 exits via NULL jump
*  Minimal W-1 witness (2026-08-07f): the match runs CORRECTLY, the proc
*  RETURNS, following statements run — the process then dies at final exit
*  (jmp to 0 from generated code; SCRIP_NO_SEGV_HANDLER=1 bt frame #0 = 0x0).
*  '*U' in place of the plain ref crashes identically; literal-only patterns,
*  RPOS/LEN/BREAK + '. U' capture in the same proc position are all CLEAN.
*  MODE SPLIT: mode-4 is rc=0 with correct output — m3-only defect.
	DEFINE('R(U)')	:(R_END)
R	'145' U	:F(FRETURN)
	R = 'OK'	:(RETURN)
R_END
	OUTPUT = R(4)
	OUTPUT = 'AFTER'
END
